{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q96D42","secondaryAccessions":["O43656"],"uniProtkbId":"HAVR1_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2005-08-30","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2019-04-10","entryVersion":178,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Hepatitis A virus cellular receptor 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"HAVcr-1"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Kidney injury molecule 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"KIM-1"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"T-cell immunoglobulin and mucin domain-containing protein 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"TIMD-1"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"T-cell immunoglobulin mucin receptor 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"TIM"},{"value":"TIM-1"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"T-cell membrane protein 1"}}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD365"}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"HAVCR1"},"synonyms":[{"value":"KIM1"},{"value":"TIM1"},{"value":"TIMD1"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q5QNS5"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17471468"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18082433"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18414680"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24703780"}],"value":"Phosphatidylserine receptor that plays an important functional role in regulatory B-cell homeostasis including generation, expansion and suppressor functions (PubMed:18082433, PubMed:18414680). Involved in efferocytosis, the process by which apoptotic cells are removed, by binding to phosphatidylserine present on apoptotic cells and promoting their engulfment (PubMed:18082433). Confers phagocytic ability on injured kidney epithelial cells, allowing them to bind to and internalize apoptotic bodies and necrotic debris following kidney injury (PubMed:17471468, PubMed:18414680). The ectodomain binds to the surface of apoptotic kidney epithelial cells via phosphatidylserine and oxidized phospholipids exposed on the cell membrane of the apoptotic cells (PubMed:18414680). HAVCR1-expressing cells are also capable of phagocytosing Gram-negative and Gram-positive bacteria (PubMed:18414680). As P-selectin/SELPLG ligand, plays a specialized role in activated but not naive T-cell trafficking during inflammatory responses (PubMed:24703780). Controls thereby T-cell accumulation in the inflamed central nervous system (CNS) and the induction of autoimmune disease (PubMed:24703780). Acts as a regulator of T-cell proliferation (By similarity). Also regulates expression of various anti-inflammatory cytokines and co-inhibitory ligands including IL10 (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29437974"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9658108"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for Hepatitis A virus"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21536871"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26487564"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for Ebolavirus and Marburg virus by binding exposed phosphatidyl-serine at the surface of virion membrane (PubMed:21536871). Serves as a dual receptor for Ebolavirus by also interacting with envelope glycoprotein GP (PubMed:26487564)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23084921"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29742433"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for Dengue virus by binding exposed phosphatidyl-serine at the surface of virion membrane (PubMed:23084921). TIM1 and Dengue virus are co-internalized during virus entry (PubMed:29742433)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"32641828"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for Zika virus by binding to envelope protein E"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"34359995"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Plays a positive role in Chikungunya virus cell entry"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24703780"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26726878"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29742433"}],"value":"Interacts with STAM (PubMed:29742433). Interacts with SELPLG (PubMed:24703780). Interacts with CD5L; interaction of HAVCR1 expressed on the surface of injured kidney tubular epithelial cells with CD5L promotes HAVCR1-mediated phagocytosis of intraluminal necrotic debris and contributes to kidney tissue repair (PubMed:26726878)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29437974"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9658108"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with hepatitis A virus capsid proteins"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26487564"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Ebolavirus envelope glycoprotein GP"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26487564"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Zika virus envelope protein E"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q96D42","intActId":"EBI-953786"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q06418","geneName":"TYRO3","intActId":"EBI-3951628"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q96D42","intActId":"EBI-953786"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P0DTC2","geneName":"S","intActId":"EBI-25474821"},"numberOfExperiments":7,"organismDiffer":true}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29742433"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Single-pass type I membrane protein","id":"SL-9905"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18414680"}],"value":"Cell projection, phagocytic cup","id":"SL-0473"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18414680"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic vesicle, phagosome","id":"SL-0206"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9658108"}],"value":"Widely expressed, with highest levels in kidney and testis. Expressed by activated CD4+ T-cells during the development of helper T-cells responses"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17471468"}],"value":"Up-regulated in the kidney in renal diseases (at protein level)"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29742433"}],"value":"Ubiquitinated at two lysine residues Lys-338 and Lys-346 on its cytoplasmic domain. Ubiquitination promotes receptor endocytosis and target receptors for lysosomal degradation and termination of receptor signaling"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29742433"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Ubiquitination is required for Dengue virus endocytosis"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14534576"}],"value":"The region containing tandem repeats is polymorphic and the sequence shown here corresponds to the most common allele (PubMed:14534576). An association between hepatitis A virus (HAV) infection and atopic diseases has been observed in individuals with that allele (PubMed:14534576). Allelic variation does not affect HAV-infection rates in Caucasians, Asians and African Americans (PubMed:14534576)"}],"commentType":"POLYMORPHISM"},{"texts":[{"value":"The extracellular part of the protein can be cleaved and detected in urine and is in correlation with the expression in the kidney"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the immunoglobulin superfamily. TIM family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":20,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":21,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":364,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Hepatitis A virus cellular receptor 1","featureId":"PRO_0000014981"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":21,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":295,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Extracellular","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":296,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":316,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":317,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":364,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Cytoplasmic","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":21,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":121,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Ig-like V-type"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start"